# Moth Template title @#title

-- this is Markdown body text, not a Moth comment.

Backslashes such as \ remain body text, while `inline [name] code` uses paired backticks.

[p:
    This paragraph is parsed as a nested Moth template inside the implicit `$md` body.

    - This nested body uses Markdown list highlighting. @#nested
    1. Ordered items also highlight.

    **Bold** and *italic* text with a [name] interpolation.

    See @./guide (Guide) and @#title (Top).

    [child:
        * Deeper templates also default to Markdown.

        # Heading in a child template
    ]
]

[
    section,
    $md:
    ## Multiline template heads remain Markdown

    This remains Markdown.
]

[raw_content, $raw:
    - This explicit formatter does not use Markdown list highlighting.
    Nested [name] templates still resolve.
]

[escaped_content, $escape_html:
    <strong>This is escaped content with [name].</strong>
]

[$note:
    This is discarded template content with [balanced] brackets.
]

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    @docs/pages/home render as render_home
    sample = "[not a template]"
    nested = [not_a_template]
    io.line([: Hello, [name]])
]

[codeblock, $code "rust":
    fn main() {
        println!("Hello, world!");
    }
]

Literal delimiters use string insertion: ["[literal]"]

